# QA And Commit Gates

- After implementation tasks, run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` when relevant to the touched area and report the result clearly.
- When touching TrainingPeaks parser, intent, digest, or attention logic, also run the relevant focused `check-*` scripts when they exist.
- Do not use `git add .` or `git add -A`. Stage explicit files only.
- Do not commit or push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Before any commit, report `git status`, the exact files changed, checks run, known risks, and anything intentionally deferred.
- Never commit `.env` files, local artifacts, debug exports, local browser state, athlete data backups, tokens, or secrets.
- If lint/build failures are unrelated to the scoped change, say so clearly instead of expanding scope silently.
